out->resize(num);
out->shrink_to_fit();
OPENSSL_memcpy(out->data(), CBS_data(&child), num * sizeof(T));
```

`resize(num)` for `std::vector<int>` value-initializes all elements to 0. Then `memcpy` copies `num * sizeof(int)` bytes. So all elements are initialized.

Wait, but what about `out->shrink_to_fit()`? This is a non-binding request. But it doesn't change the size of the vector, only potentially the capacity. So all elements are still initialized.

